h2 { "How to read the reference" }

Each entry describes accepted inputs, result, placement and failures. T, U, F and dimension letters are explanatory placeholders, not supported generic declarations. Overloads share one entry. A static type/shape mistake is diagnosed at compile time; dynamic bounds, shape, arithmetic and resource failures are checked during execution. TaskError is recoverable at task boundaries; not every checked failure is an application error channel on a direct call.

link { url = "/docs/language-reference", "Types, constructors, operators and error syntax" }
link { url = "/docs/tooling", "Compiler, checker, formatter and editor commands" }

h2 { "Program output and external libraries" }

The command-line executable displays the value returned by main. There is no built-in print or general file/network I/O function in this interface. Packages can export their own functions; those names belong to the package rather than this built-in index.

link { url = "/docs/packages", "Using source packages" }
